# Text, stored with LF and checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows installs with `core.autocrlf` on, which would check the tree
# out with CRLF while the repository holds LF — so a Windows working copy would
# not be byte-for-byte what CI checks out and builds, and a diff that looks like
# nothing becomes every line. The tests read mangaTools.css and the bundle as
# text; pinning the ending keeps what they read the same here as there.
* text=auto eol=lf
